+e2631net command
+================
+
+Synopsis
+--------
+
+::
+
+    e2631net
+
+Description
+-----------
+
+The *e2631net* command prints the state of the U-Boot Ethernet driver on the
+ZTE ZXHN E2631 (Sanechips ZX279128S).  It reports the switch port and PHY the
+driver is bound to, whether the PHY has a link and at which speed and duplex,
+the MAC control and traffic-manager interrupt registers, the number of free
+BMU buffers, the completed TX count and the occupancy of the eight RX queues.
+
+The command is read-only: it writes no register and sends no packet, so it can
+be used before *dhcp* or *tftp* to check that the cable, PHY and switch port
+are ready and to find out which switch port the link is on.
+
+The driver is built only for the ZX279128S port (``CONFIG_ETH_ZX279128S``).
+On this board it drives the port the board routes to lan1, which is switch
+port 2 and PHY 12 (MDIO address 0x0c); the same PHY can be inspected with
+*mii info* and *mii read*.
+
+Example
+-------
+
+::
+
+    => e2631net
+    e2631net: lan1 switch port 2, started
+    e2631net: PHY 12 link up, 1000 Mbit/s full duplex
+    e2631net: MAC ctrl 0x00bbe000, TM int 0x00000000, BMU free 0x0000fffe, TX done 0
+    e2631net: RX queue counts 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
